WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.010
If you follow me on twitter you know I'm not
a big fan of awards shows in general, but

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:14.130
all the talk post Golden Globes is about Oprah
Winfrey potentially running for president

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.469
in 2020.

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:19.960
Mainstream media is in love with the idea
of Oprah for President, and CNN, the NY Times,

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:26.400
Time Magazine, and others have all run think
pieces on her chances in just three years

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.400
from now.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.989
Hollywood of course is also love with the
idea.. the conscience of lefty hollywood Jimmy

00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:36.510
Kimmel has already said that he's on board
with Oprah 2020, and NBC even tweeted from

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:42.149
their official account that Oprah is our next
president...though they eventually deleted

00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:43.199
the tweet.

00:00:43.199 --> 00:00:48.750
Make no doubt, the elite class that was dealt
a swift blow by the election of Trump in 2016

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:53.639
will quickly fall in line if Oprah decides
to make a run.

00:00:53.639 --> 00:00:58.179
Oprah has a remarkable life story -- she grew
up in a Milwaukee boarding house in extreme

00:00:58.179 --> 00:01:03.960
poverty, surviving absolutely horrific physical
and sexual abuse, including being raped by

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.170
her cousin when she was only 9 years old.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:12.000
From these unimaginably difficult beginnings,
Oprah eventually made it into local news in

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.990
Chicago and then onto her syndicated talk
show which not only changed the TV landscape

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:21.820
but had a cultural relevance unlike almost
anything in the pre-internet age.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:27.299
Every politician, pop culture figure and ordinary
person doing something extraordinary seemed

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:29.540
to make it to Oprah's couch.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:34.040
Since she ended the talk show 7 years ago,
Oprah's had many professional ups and downs

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:40.010
continuing to navigate hollywood, starting
her TV network OWN which hasn't really caught

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:46.409
on, charity work, and of course always making
time to eat bread with very excited strangers

00:01:46.409 --> 00:01:49.520
around a fancy table in a forest.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:55.070
As for Oprah's politics, I'm not sure anyone
other Oprah herself has a full view of them.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:02:00.189
She was a big Obama supporter during his two
campaigns and I have no doubt she's falls

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:03.100
on the Democrat-progressive side of things.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:08.180
How she falls specifically on every issue
I'm not totally sure, but we seem to be veering

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:14.220
towards a cliff where the issues will have
almost nothing to do with who gets elected.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:18.760
The cult of personality we're building around
politicians and what that means for the health

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:24.220
of our society in the long term is quickly
becoming a massive problem that is hidden

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.220
in plain sight.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:28.980
I'm pretty sure I don't have to say much on
the cult of personality that is Donald Trump.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:33.720
Make no mistake whether you love or hate Donald
Trump, we elected a reality TV star, a man

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.450
created by and now hated by the mainstream
media.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:42.610
Trump's rise used all the tools of the media
against itself and that's why right now the

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:47.470
media is endlessly looking to destroy him...they
want their narrative and control back.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:51.570
Notice the shift in TV coverage and articles
about Trump in the last two weeks or so, it's

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:55.480
shifted from endless Russia stories to Trump's
mental health.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:03:00.019
In most cases, the people writing these stories
are the same people who said that stories

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:05.950
about Hillary's health were conspiracy theories...even
after she collapsed and was dragged into an

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:09.580
SUV by security guards that autumn day in
New York City.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:16.190
So what we have right now is a cult of personality,
Trump, versus the cult of media.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.190
This has made a lot of people a lot of money.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:22.900
As long as they keep churning out articles
and think pieces, true or not, people get

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:23.900
paid.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:27.910
To this end, Trump is their perfect foil,
he has no shortage of Tweets to send out and

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:32.750
people to mock, so we've got a match made
in hell playing our right in front of our

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.350
eyes.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:36.299
Now back to Oprah for a moment.

00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:40.440
Oprah is basically the exact reverse of Trump,
even at the identity politics level: she is

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.360
a black woman and he is a white man.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.450
She grew up poor, he grew up rich.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:49.209
But more important than this, she says all
the right things, talks about love and spirituality,

00:03:49.209 --> 00:03:53.519
and is loved by the Hollywood and media class
as one of their own.

00:03:53.519 --> 00:03:58.799
Trump, on the other hand is their perfect
enemy, as if they had written the script themselves.

00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:03.930
Alas, Trump was one of their own until he
became too powerful and now he is enemy number

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:07.180
one because they've lost control of the narrative.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:12.110
Their hope is they can win some of that narrative
back with another celebrity who will play

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:18.370
by their rules but I think this is shortsighted
at best and disastrous at worst.

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:26.130
Just imagine what kinda of insane polarizing,
sensationalized lunacy this potential matchup

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.690
will lead to as we head into 2020.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:33.570
It'll be great for clicks and ratings, but
it'll be terrible for ideas and debate.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.180
You thought Hillary v. Trump was polarizing?

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:40.930
Just wait until Trump and Oprah battle it
out in the Thunderdome on prime time TV.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:46.200
Sadly, it doesn't look like we'll ever turn
back to being governed as our founders intended,

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:51.220
with a limited federal government and strong
states that empower people to control their

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.100
lives at the local level.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:57.700
While Trump has done some good work in limited
the power of the federal government, he's

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:03.360
obviously happy to govern by executive action
as congress cedes more and more of their duties

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:09.060
to the executive branch, instead of the legislative
branch where laws are supposed to be written.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:13.340
His justice department too, is happy to step
on the 10th Amendment and allow the federal

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:18.210
government to trample on states rights, just
look at Attorney General Jeff Sessions decision

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:22.890
to allow the feds to crack down on states
ability to legalize marijuana.

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:26.560
So to sum up, we’ll have a president that
will most likely be a celebrity, whether it's

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:31.300
Trump or Oprah or Mark Cuban or The Rock,
along with a executive branch that will continue

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.400
growing and growing in power.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:38.170
This cult of personality will continually
put people into office not on what they believe

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:42.870
and whether they understand or even care how
government is supposed to work, but rather

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:47.950
by what they make us feel and how they can
manipulate us into thinking exactly as they

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:48.950
do.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:53.940
That feeling, coupled with that growing power
of the office of the president is a recipe

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:57.750
for the authoritarian control we should all
be wary of.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:03.620
The only way to fight the tide of this celebrity
induced Idiocracy is to get involved now before

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:04.840
it's too late.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:09.479
Either that, or get ready to bow to Supreme
Leader Justin Bieber in 2024.

